//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// AGITQ 161-day MA TQQQ strategy — TradingView backtest
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Rules (from the r/TQQQ "ultimate TQQQ strategy" post):
//   * Signal is driven by QQQ, NOT by TQQQ.
//   * QQQ closes ABOVE its 161-day SMA  -> hold TQQQ.
//   * QQQ closes BELOW its 161-day SMA  -> exit to cash.
//   * Overheated: QQQ > MA * (1 + 5%)   -> block NEW entries (ballast). An
//                                          existing TQQQ position keeps riding
//                                          until QQQ drops back below the MA.
//
// HOW TO USE
//   1. Open a TQQQ chart on the Daily (1D) timeframe.
//   2. Open the Pine Editor, paste this whole file, click "Add to chart".
//   3. Open the "Strategy Tester" tab to see net profit, drawdown, trades.
//   4. Optional: tune MA length / overheated band via the strategy's gear icon.
//
// WHY request.security(): the strategy trades the chart symbol (TQQQ) but the
// signal must come from QQQ's own 161-day average, so we fetch QQQ separately.
// =============================================================================

strategy(
     title                   = "AGITQ 161MA (QQQ signal, trade TQQQ)",
     overlay                 = true,
     initial_capital         = 10000,
     default_qty_type        = strategy.percent_of_equity,
     default_qty_value       = 100,
     commission_type         = strategy.commission.percent,
     commission_value        = 0.0,
     calc_on_every_tick      = false,
     process_orders_on_close = true)

// --- Timeframe guard ---------------------------------------------------------
// This strategy is designed for the DAILY chart. On weekly/monthly there are
// too few bars (you'll see only a handful of trades); on intraday it's noisy.
// A wrong timeframe is the #1 cause of "why so few trades?". Warn loudly.
if not timeframe.isdaily and barstate.islast
    runtime.error("Apply this strategy on the DAILY (1D) timeframe. Current "
         + "timeframe is '" + timeframe.period + "'. Switch the chart to 1D.")

// --- Inputs ------------------------------------------------------------------
maLen       = input.int(161,   "MA length (days)", minval = 2)
overheatPct = input.float(5.0, "Overheated band (%)", minval = 0.0) / 100.0
signalSym   = input.symbol("NASDAQ:QQQ", "Signal symbol (index proxy)")
blockOnHot  = input.bool(true, "Block new entries when overheated")

// --- Signal series (QQQ) — independent of the chart symbol -------------------
// Compute the MA and the regime flags INSIDE the QQQ daily context and request
// the finished values. Requesting the fully-computed signal (not just raw close)
// is the multi-timeframe-safe pattern: it works whether the chart is daily or
// intraday, and can't be distorted by resolution mismatch. lookahead_off keeps
// us on confirmed daily closes only (no look-ahead bias).
[qqqClose, qqqMa, aboveMa, overheated] = request.security(
     signalSym, "D",
     [close,
      ta.sma(close, maLen),
      close > ta.sma(close, maLen),
      close > ta.sma(close, maLen) * (1.0 + overheatPct)],
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

// --- Trading rules -----------------------------------------------------------
// Enter TQQQ when QQQ is above the MA and not overheated; exit to cash below MA.
enterLong = aboveMa and not (blockOnHot and overheated)
exitLong  = not aboveMa

if enterLong
    strategy.entry("Long TQQQ", strategy.long)

if exitLong
    strategy.close("Long TQQQ", comment = "QQQ < MA")

// --- Visuals -----------------------------------------------------------------
// Regime background: red = QQQ below MA (cash), orange = overheated (ballast).
// This works on ANY chart symbol and is the clearest at-a-glance signal.
bgcolor(not aboveMa ? color.new(color.red,    88) : na, title = "Below MA (cash)")
bgcolor(overheated  ? color.new(color.orange, 88) : na, title = "Overheated (ballast)")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SHOWING QQQ PRICE + ITS 161-MA
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The honest constraint: this strategy trades TQQQ (~$50-140) but the signal is
// QQQ (~$400-600). On a TQQQ chart, QQQ's REAL price/MA would plot far off the
// top and be invisible. A single Pine script also can't open a second pane. So
// there are two ways to see QQQ and its 161-MA at their TRUE values:
//
//   BEST — chart QQQ directly:  set `chartOnQqq = true` below AND change the
//   chart symbol to NASDAQ:QQQ. Then the candles ARE QQQ, and the real 161-MA +
//   overheated band plot exactly on price. The strategy still trades a 3x proxy
//   for the tester. This is the recommended way to VISUALISE the signal.
//
//   ON A TQQQ CHART — the QQQ MA is rescaled by the live TQQQ/QQQ ratio so it
//   tracks near the TQQQ candles (a visual aid; the signal uses the true MA).
//
// Either way the trade signal is identical — only the drawing differs.
chartOnQqq = input.bool(false,
     "I'm charting QQQ (plot REAL QQQ price + MA). Leave OFF for a TQQQ chart.")
showMa     = input.bool(true, "Show QQQ 161-MA")
showBand   = input.bool(true, "Show overheated (+5%) band")

// True-value lines (use when the chart symbol IS QQQ).
qqqBandTrue = qqqMa * (1.0 + overheatPct)

// Rescaled lines (use on a TQQQ chart so they land near the candles).
scaleFactor = close / qqqClose
maRescaled  = qqqMa * scaleFactor
bandRescaled = qqqBandTrue * scaleFactor

// Pick which set to draw based on the chart the user is on.
maPlot   = chartOnQqq ? qqqMa : maRescaled
bandPlot = chartOnQqq ? qqqBandTrue : bandRescaled

// Also plot QQQ's real close when charting QQQ (redundant with the candles, but
// confirms request.security is returning live data — handy for sanity checks).
// plot() titles must be CONST strings (known at compile time), so they can't be
// a ternary. Titles are fixed; whether the value is real or rescaled depends on
// the `chartOnQqq` toggle (see the maPlot/bandPlot definitions above).
plot(chartOnQqq ? qqqClose : na, "QQQ close",
     color = color.new(color.blue, 40), linewidth = 1)
plot(showMa ? maPlot : na, "QQQ 161-MA",
     color = color.new(color.orange, 0), linewidth = 2)
plot(showBand ? bandPlot : na, "QQQ MA +5% band",
     color = color.new(color.red, 30), linewidth = 1, style = plot.style_stepline)
